NOTES (web fidelity, no scope narrowing)
  - The web page gates the WHOLE surface on combined vehicles+analytics loading/error (isLoading =
    vehiclesLoading || analyticsLoading, error = vehiclesError || analyticsError) and reads vehicle = vehicles?.[0].
    mergeQuickStats (QuickStatsPageModel.kt:231) folds the two cache-then-network Resources into one UiState exactly
    so: either first-loading → Loading, either hard error → Error, otherwise Content (or Empty when no first vehicle).
  - The four metric cards always render their (possibly zero) fleet totals from the independent analytics feed in BOTH
    the Empty and Content phases — exactly like the web, which renders the grid regardless of the noVehicle panel.
  - Empty-state divergence (Honesty Covenant #9, documented): the web shows the noVehicle EmptyState inside the vehicle
    GlassPanel; the native surface routes that case to UiPhase.Empty so the panel shows the same friendly empty-state
    (QuickStatsPage.kt:208) while the metric grid still renders — making all 4 declared states genuinely reachable.
  - SI-canonical: total_distance_km is bridged km→m (×1000) before convertDistanceFromSI at the display boundary
    (QuickStatsDisplayPrefs.fromKm); energy (kWh), cost and counts are raw on the wire and rendered verbatim — web parity.
  - 'offline' (vehicleStateLabelOf fallback) is a raw Tesla vehicle-state value the web hard-codes as the `?? 'offline'`
    data fallback for stateData?.state?.state, not a UI string — it is correctly NOT among the 9 localized keys.
  - a11y: merged-descendant semantics + contentDescription on the vehicle panel (QuickStatsPage.kt:226) and each metric
    card (QuickStatsPage.kt:300); the footer link is a Material 3 Button (automatic ≥48dp target). Dark/dynamic theme +
    SI honored; Compose-native only (no webview).

